# Every path has an owner, so a pull request always requests a review from
# someone. muxtop has a single maintainer today; the per-area lines below are
# not redundant duplication — they are where a second reviewer gets added when
# one shows up, without having to rediscover the boundaries.

*                           @lucasschimmel

# Security-relevant surface: the network-facing daemon, the wire protocol, the
# process-signalling module, and the dependency allow-list.
/crates/muxtop-server/      @lucasschimmel
/crates/muxtop-proto/       @lucasschimmel
/crates/muxtop-core/src/actions.rs  @lucasschimmel
/deny.toml                  @lucasschimmel

# Anything that can publish, sign, or grant permissions.
/.github/workflows/         @lucasschimmel
/.github/dependabot.yml     @lucasschimmel
/scripts/install.sh         @lucasschimmel

# Documentation that users act on — a wrong command here is a real incident.
/SECURITY.md                @lucasschimmel
/docs/wiki/                 @lucasschimmel
